WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 line:92%
-Hey, Jim, welcome to the show

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.503 line:92%
-Wow. Good afternoon, Seth

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
It's good to be here.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I want to ask
about this show...

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...which is about your fora

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:13.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
into cannabis farming,
but I want to start by asking,

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:17.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
how did you decide
to become a cannabis farmer?

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.785 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Totally by accident.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got this really
sweet little property

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the Rogue River
in Southern Oregon.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the property behind me
is an 80-acre farm.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.563 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it came up for sale.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
I bought it.
And I was like, uh, now what

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, hay, alfalfa,
corn, cattle.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it just so happened
that the cannabis was lega

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the state of Oregon
just that year,

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.277 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and I went, "Well..."

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Got a couple guys,

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:49.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
one Captain Jack who used to b
the weed dealer

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.485 line:92%
at "SNL" in the early '70s

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really exciting
because I do think you worry

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
that with the legalization
of cannabis

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.627 size:75% position:38%
that it might become
a little corporate.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.362 size:88% position:44%
It's really nice to know
that you're working with

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
a guy named Captain Jack.
-Captain Jack.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, there are no corporate
guys in the field.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:10.170 line:92%
They're all old-time growers

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Old spiritual creatures.
Agriculturalists.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really natural,
natural ingredients.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.414
The corporate guys kind of cam
in to see where the money is

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
but...and now I've become
one of them.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you look --
I will say, you do not --

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
laying eyes on you,
I am not in any way worrie

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:30.790 line:92%
that you've gone corporate

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
You look very --
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
You look way more like
a guy who'd be hanging out

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Captain Jack than --
-Yeah.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:41.134
-Do you name -- do you help name
the different strains, Jim

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:44.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I have one -- we have
about six, seven strains.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one is Captain Jack's,
of course.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
We call it the Smell of "SNL."
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because that's what it wa
known as back then,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.447 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the Smell of "SNL."

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.484
Because it was the hallways,
you know, in the early '70s.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:58.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure. Sure.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:02.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have one called Cherry Pi
that I really like, Seth,

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.291 line:92%
because it's a very low THC.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's like 18%.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.661 line:92%
But it has like 3% terpenes,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:12.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is the flavor
and the smell.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.700 line:92%
And with a little bit of CBD

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.637
the three of them create wha
they call an entourage effect.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which is just kind of
this calming,

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's no anxiety
and there's no paranoia.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can still be chill
and sweet.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:27.046 line:92%
Actually, I named it because

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would come downstairs
at night,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my wife would go,
"Are you hungry?"

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd go, "Yeah." And she goes
"Let's go out to eat."

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.855
"Okay." "What do you have
a taste for?", she'd say?

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went --
well, I'm from Chicago,

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.958 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I wanted cheeseburgers.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.795 size:88% position:44%
She goes, "Oh, Jim, it's
a little heavy for me.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Anything else?"

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, how about some sushi?
"Oh.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had sushi with my mom
last night.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:50.470 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Anything else?"

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, how about if we go to
a natural food --"

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.407 line:92%
"Cilantro, cilantro, cilantro,

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.742 line:92%
they put cilantro everything."

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you wasting
my time for?

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know we're going to ea
where you want to eat

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
and eat
what you want to eat!"

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.652 line:92%
-So now I take one little hit,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.621
because I'm a microdoser,
I only take one little bit

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.858
-Yeah.
-I come downstairs and she says,

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Are you hungry?"
"Yeah."

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You want to go out to eat?"
"Sure."

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.628 line:92%
"Where do you want to go?"

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Baby, we can go
to Taco Bell

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:19.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
as long as you're sitting
across from me.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:20.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ah, see?
-And she's like --

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What a great
advertisement.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Aren't you being charming?
Right?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.808
And so I call that strain
the Marriage Counselor.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, the Marriage Counselor.
That is...

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I told that story in Oregon
Seth,

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.882 line:92%
and it sold out in two months.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't even keep it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Women are coming
into dispensaries --

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:40.853 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Very good marketing.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they come into
dispensaries and say,

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Where's that
Marriage Counselor?

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He needs some."

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on the other end,
I have a thing

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:52.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
called Black Diamond,
which the veterans really like

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:58.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it helps with the PTSD
and pain and sleep.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.639 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And especially the PTSD.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of my friends
is paralyzed

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:06.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the chest down
and his legs go into spasms.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:12.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this Black Diamond
stops those spasms.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.019 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And so it's really --

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a lot of medicinal
properties to this.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I call that one
Assisted Living.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is -- well,
you're obviously providing

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:21.694 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a service there.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:26.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're also real world
philanthropic --

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
I should say efforts.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you talk a little bit abou
the Last Prisoner Project?

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I think it's a reall
great organization

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:35.642
that's taking into account
that what used to be illegal

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:38.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
is now not, and yet there'
still plenty of people

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:41.114 line:92%
serving jail time for marijuana.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.650 line:92%
-Seth, there's 40,000 prisoner

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are serving jail time
for non-violent

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:49.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
cannabis consumption
or possession.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a guy named
Michael Thompson in Michigan

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope the governor of Michiga
is watching this.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Please release him.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
He got sentenced
to 40 to 60 years

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
for having three pounds
of cannabis.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.471 line:92%
He's been in for 25 years.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is now -- we wanted
to get him out

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.909 size:81% position:41%
because we were scared
for him to get COVID.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has COVID.
He's in the hospital.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:15.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this should not be
a death sentence

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
for something that is legal,
it's medicine,

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:21.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's non-violent, and there'
thousands of prisoners.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:25.425
Steve DeAngelo and myself
and a few other people

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
are on the board,
and we're trying to get

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.394 line:92%
these people out of prison

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:32.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's always -- it's always
been communities of color

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
subject to the
disappropriateness

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.869 line:92%
of this kind of practices.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's --
So I'm part of that.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great that
you're doing that.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.776 size:88% position:44% line:92%
This is such a fun show.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:48.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really cool to see yo
behind the scenes of this farm

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:52.919
and the travels you make t
Colombia among other places.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Thanks so much for making -

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I went to Colombia
for nine days with cameras

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
and improvised
the whole time.

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:04.430
And it's probably the middle
part of our three episodes

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's on Discovery coming u
on Wednesday the 19th.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.469 size:78% position:39%
-Well, I can't wait.
And thank you so much

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:11.738
for making time for us, Jim.
Always a pleasure to see you

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, Seth, it's always
a pleasure to see you

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:18.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thank you so much
for your time.

